---
Connecting from external clients (PAT)
  Endpoints that accept PAT (e.g. PUT /settings, POST /upload, data-models auto CRUD) require a
  Personal Access Token (PAT), not the session JWT.

  • Use the PAT string that starts with "nvpat_" (e.g. nvpat_abc123...). Create it in admin:
    Organization → Personal Access Tokens → Create; copy the token once (it is not shown again).

  • Do NOT use the JWT/session token (the one that starts with "eyJ..." from login). If you send
    a JWT where a PAT is required, the API returns 401 and logs show:
      Auth: JWT decode failed for eyJhbGciOi...(121 chars): InvalidSignatureError
      PAT lookup: no row for token hash (token may be wrong or expired)
      Auth: token eyJ... -> not valid JWT and PAT lookup failed
    Fix: send the PAT (nvpat_...) in the Authorization header, not the JWT.

  • Header format:   Authorization: Bearer nvpat_YOUR_FULL_TOKEN
  • Full details and examples: see how_to_use_pat.md (§2a and §3a).

