How to run decrypt (data model field values)
  From repo root. Uses same key as app (ENCRYPTION_KEY for AES; fixed key for XOR).

  XOR:
    python3 api/decrypt_field_value.py xor_cipher "<base64_encrypted_value>"

  AES (set ENCRYPTION_KEY first, e.g. from api/.env):
    export ENCRYPTION_KEY="<your-32-byte-key-base64-or-raw>"
    python3 api/decrypt_field_value.py aes "<base64_encrypted_value>"

  With venv:
    /path/to/noolva/api/app/noolva-venv/bin/python3 api/decrypt_field_value.py aes "<value>"

---
WebSocket
  When you start the API with runserver, the WebSocket endpoint is available on the same host and port at /ws (e.g. ws://localhost:9001/ws). No separate process or port; use APPLICATION_PORT. See how-to-connect-websocket.

